<title>FRANCE: Eleven-month French grain use in feed up 8.9 pct.</title>
<headline>Eleven-month French grain use in feed up 8.9 pct.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-07-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>French cereals office ONIC released the following breakdown of grain consumption for commercial animal feed in France this season.</p>
<p>The figures, in thousands of tonnes, are for the first 11 months of the July/June season up to May 31.</p>
<p>			  Soft wheat Barley   Maize   Durum   Total</p>
<p> 1996/97 (Jul-May)    5,185.3   943.8  2,243.9   0.0   8,373.0</p>
<p> 1995/96 (Jul-May)    5,147.2   778.9  1,765.0   0.3   7,691.4</p>
<p> Percent change	    +0.7   +21.2    +27.1   ---	+8.9</p>
<p> 96/97 est. (Jul-Jun)   5,550   1,000    2,550     0     9,100</p>
<p> 95/96 (Jul-Jun)	5,583.7   867.3  1,916.5   0.3   8,367.8</p>
<p>ONIC also released the following data for non-grain feed imports between July and the end of May (thousand tonnes).</p>
<p>			   Manioc     Corn gluten	Total</p>
<p> 1996/97 (Jul-May)    96.4	   92.3	    552.0</p>
<p> 1995/96 (Jul-May)    79.3	  236.9	    688.3</p>
<p>--Paris newsroom +331 4221 5432</p>
</text>
